+# Work Harness C/D implementation record
+
+Owner approved implementation of the C/D math-code loop and local installation.
+Source parent: 33c4a12ba0045c3000a699858b90fdf869ea74ed.
+
+## Delivered behavior
+
+- Explicit work-harness-cd-v1 profile; same 84 identities, versioned C/D catalog and 17 node overrides.
+- C diagnoses condition mismatch, real failure or unnecessarily strict dependencies with actual interventions and native evaluation.
+- D derives and implements mechanisms, tests qualified comparisons and falsifiable predictions on real existing assets.
+- Reviewer-approved targeted B visits return to origin; C/D revisions invalidate the dependent active suffix while retaining immutable history, jobs and usage.
+- B05 and M05 require actual collected native predictions joined to protocol/arm/group/seed and controller receipts, followed by fixed native scorer replay and independent review.
+- M05 binds the full treatment code set and pending E coverage obligations. Verified acceptance automatically advances to E. E keeps formal design/fairness/freeze/confirmation.
+- B01 official setup/owner-authorized baseline qualification remains supported. Other plugin editions and omitted-profile semantics remain unchanged.
+- Explicit quiet-boundary adoption with SQLite recovery backup, source pins, revision CAS and retained legacy acceptances.
+
+## GPU verification
+
+All implementation tests/builds ran on the authorized hn01 GPU host in isolated code-tests/cd-flow, not on the Mac or production research directory. These are software fixtures, not scientific findings.
+
+- Final stable-source focused suite: 70 tests passed (C/D flow/admission/scoring plus B01 setup/qualification).
+- Plugin suite: 34 passed. Node inventory: 84 nodes, 221 edges, no errors.
+- Whole runtime suite: 367 tests, 8 failures. Seven legacy admission failures reproduce at exact parent HEAD; CLI timing/reconciliation case passes on separate six-test rerun. No timing guarantee is claimed.
+- Whole Skill suite: 930 tests, eight legacy policy failures and two missing-SciPy errors, nine skipped. Exact parent reproduces the same eight failures and two dependency errors. Dependency installation/statistics rerun is recorded separately when completed.
+- Earlier focused attempt hit source-pin protection during concurrent inventory refresh; final stable-source rerun passes. This is retained in logs rather than relabeled.
+- Package builder initially rejected an overlong default prompt; metadata corrected and ZIP build succeeded.
+
+## Independent review and rulings
+
+Fresh independent whole-change review found two important issues: scored manifests lacked a strict join to actual collected outputs, and B01 qualification was overconstrained by the general development route. Both corrected with GPU regression tests (16 admission tests). Earlier integration review also corrected inherited cycle audits, B visit classification, unscored gate acceptance and unenforced E obligation IDs.
+
+Ruling: preserve old profile behavior and failures rather than weaken scientific guards to satisfy stale legacy fixtures. Costs/limitations are visible above.
+Ruling: retiring a completed but unreviewed old-profile transport at a quiet maintenance boundary does not accept its science; archive full state and terminal receipts first.
+Ruling: installation and live adoption are separate receipts, performed only after this source is committed. This source report does not itself claim either action happened.
+
+## Operations
+
+The source runtime is installed separately from the skills-only ZIP. The authorized live project uses existing SSH target and model/data environment; installation must preserve local plugin identity research-autopilot-harness. Record source commit, installed cache identity, immutable adoption receipt and observed new worker packet in the SPECTRUM delivery report. No aggregate budget/round caps or GitHub Actions were introduced.
