+# Work Harness C/D runtime contracts
+
+Apply only to `work-harness-cd-v1`. Every `*_ref` is a real project-relative
+`{path, sha256}` pin. Use unique immutable paths per revision; never invent a hash.
+The controller supplies `sequence` including profile, epoch, problem and verified
+handoff pins. Copy the entire binding unchanged. The exact runtime schema wins.
+
+## Decisions and task inputs
+
+`research-cd-decision`, `schema_version: 1` fields:
+`goal_id`, `previous_ref` (accepted predecessor or null at intake), `stage`
+(`diagnosis`, `development`, `scaleup`), `rationale`, `selected_task_ids` (exact
+proposal task IDs, [] for acceptance), `evidence_refs`, `observed_receipt_refs`
+(all previously observed and all fresh native receipts), `problem_ref`,
+`mechanism_ref`, `verified_ref` (explicit null when not applicable).
+The first C/D decision may extend the exact accepted legacy v4 decision. Never
+rewrite a v4 artifact as though it had always had the new meaning.
+
+Scientific child tasks bind `reasoning_ref`, `goal_id`, `candidate_id`,
+`research_scope` diagnostic for C/B reproduction or method for D, and
+`cd_evidence_ref`. C/D native jobs use `native_purpose: development`.
+
+B01 remains the explicit setup exception: an already owner-authorized
+baseline qualification uses `native_purpose: qualification`, its actual
+authorization/instruction/target pins and baseline-only arms. It cannot carry
+a treatment or substitute for C's comparative diagnosis or D's method evidence.
+
+`cd_evidence_ref` is `kind: research-cd-experiment`, `schema_version: 1` with:
+`flow_profile`, `stage`, `candidate_id`, `goal_id`, `question`, `assumptions`
+(nonempty text list), `mathematical_object`, `prediction`, `falsifier`, `code_plan`,
+`code_bindings` ({mathematical_object, code_ref, location} list), `benchmark_ref`,
+`model_ref`, `dataset_ref`, `evaluation_ref`, `controls`
+({name, rationale, implementation_refs} list), `uncertainty_plan`,
+`exposure_log_ref`, `condition_source_refs`, `problem_ref`, `mechanism_ref`.
+Code creation may start with empty code_bindings; native work must have real
+mapped code and executed baseline/intervention/control arms. Diagnosis remains
+scientific development even when it rejects the hypothesis.
+
+Native plans retain standard scientific protocol/scorer/coverage/transfer rules.
+Use `evidence_mode: developmental`; native provenance binds `cd_evidence_ref`.
+Protocol `cd_development` is exactly `{flow_profile, stage, cd_evidence_ref}`.
+Do not mix legacy method_discovery into this development route. A successful
+training/export receipt with deferred scoring cannot close a scientific gate.
+
+## Result and revisit fields
+
+The standard current-step result retains all existing fields. The profile adds
+optional `revisit_request` or `cd_gate_ref`; never combine a revisit with child
+tasks or a gate. A revisit has `mode`, `origin` (full sequence binding), `target`,
+`return_to`, `reason`, `expected_output`, `evidence_refs`. `visit` targets one of
+L01/L02/L03/X02/L04/X03/L05 and returns to the origin node. `revise` targets an
+earlier/current C/D node and uses `return_to: null`. Review approval must judge
+the specific request; unfinished origin requirements are not marked satisfied.
+
+## C problem gate
+
+B05 tasks=[] without revisit must cite `cd_gate_ref`, kind
+`research-cd-problem`, schema_version 1:
+`goal_id`, `version`, `method`, `conditions`, `dependency_or_failure`,
+`assumptions`, `observables`, `competing_explanations`, `intervention`,
+`consequences`, `uncertainty` (nonempty explanatory text), `evidence_refs`,
+`run_receipt_refs`, `scored_runs`.
+Actual run receipts are controller-archived native executions, including their
+retained source/output pins. `scored_runs` is a nonempty list of
+`{protocol_ref, manifest_ref}` for actual completed canonical native manifests.
+Each arm prediction pin must match a declared, collected and archived output of
+a cited native execution with the same protocol, arm role, group and seed. A
+manifest assembled later is allowed; unrelated/manually substituted predictions
+are not evidence of that run. Declare prediction outputs before execution.
+The fixed verifier replays the existing scorer on the pinned GPU target before
+independent acceptance. A low measured quality in C can be a real failure;
+reviewer still checks implementation and baseline competence before supporting it.
+
+## D scaleup gate
+
+M05 tasks=[] without revisit must cite `cd_gate_ref`, kind
+`research-cd-scaleup`, schema_version 1:
+`goal_id`, `problem_ref` (current accepted C contract), `mechanism_ref`,
+`candidate_id`, `code_ref`, `method_code_refs`, `protocol_ref`, `run_receipt_refs`, `analysis_refs`,
+`exposure_ref`, `scored_runs`, `e_obligations`, `obligations`.
+
+`obligations` contains exactly one `{id, finding, evidence_refs}` for each:
+- problem_supported
+- math_code_correspondence
+- real_benchmark_comparison
+- strong_simple_controls
+- mechanism_prediction
+- uncertainty_and_practical_effect
+- confounds_checked
+- nearest_work
+- negative_results_and_exposure
+- scope_and_e_obligations
+
+`e_obligations` contains distinct IDs from the successor coverage snapshot, still
+pending or blocked. Retain full confirmation, scale, transfer and repetition
+requirements as appropriate to the claim. Prose outside coverage is insufficient.
+The fixed native verifier checks scored_runs; reviewer then judges whether the
+measured effect and mechanism evidence warrant scaling. Valid JSON, exit0,
+non-significant differences, isolated winning examples and unscored exports do
+not establish VERIFIED_FOR_SCALEUP.
+
+## E handoff
+
+The method_code_refs array pins the complete treatment code set, including code_ref.
+Changing this set requires a reviewed D revision; E may vary protocol parameters
+and data while keeping the accepted method implementation fixed.
+
+Program records the M05 acceptance and actual builtin scoring verification,
+then automatically advances to S02. Formal protocol uses `cd_scaleup` exactly
+`{flow_profile, verified_ref, acceptance_ref}` from trusted sequence binding;
+`cd_problem_ref` equals its accepted problem. E comparison must use the accepted
+method code and formal evidence mode; development data exposure remains visible.
+Preserve formal method/code/design validation, fair S04, freezing, full coverage,
+actual native scorer replay and scientific closure. The handoff replaces old
+Gate0/IPCG prerequisites, not E confirmation evidence.
